  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community water contamination treatment and environmental remediation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This one-year project will improve access to clean water for Bolivian highland communities in the middle and lower Katari River basins, specifically in the municipalities of Laja and Pucarani. By introducing innovative, low-cost water treatment technologies and fostering collaboration between local communities, universities, and civil society, the initiative will enable three communities to obtain safe water for household use, agriculture, and livestock-directly enhancing their livelihoods and wellbeing. 
With support from a major donor, it plans community workshops with a focus on inclusion and gender equality, technical feasibility studies, the implementation of nature-based water purification technologies (such as fog catchers, biochar, and microalgae), and knowledge sharing between Bolivian and UK partners. The project also emphasizes the importance of replicating successful approaches by sharing experiences with local governments and producing academic outputs to inform broader environmental management efforts.</narrative>
  </description>
